  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Balkans Integrated Border Management Facility (WBIBM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to support the authorities in Montenegro to effectively manage their borders and respond to border security challenges mindful of migrant protection principles, through the Western Balkans Integrated Border Management Capacity Building Facility (WBIBM). The increasingly complex mixed migration dynamics in the Western Balkans (WB), coupled with the operational challenges caused by the COVID-19 pandemic since the beginning of 2020, have revealed important institutional needs and gaps in the field of border management and border security in the region. Within the Montenegro Concept Note, a unified training package on humanitarian border management (HBM) and protection-sensitive registration, referral and reception of migrants at points of entry, was developed to be followed by two roll out trainings at the national level. This project will cover one, out of the two trainings with a focus on Border Police officers at the first line at the border, who are directly in charge of protection-sensitive registration, referral and reception of migrants at points of entry, hence complementing the entire HBM component envisaged under the WBIBM concept note for Montenegro.</narrative>
  </description>
